---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
    title="Devices"
    current="devices"
    description="GPX and FIT courses for a watch, a GPS, or a bike computer."
>
    <main class="wrap page">
        <p class="kicker">Devices</p>
        <h1>The device already knows the map.</h1>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                Export a GPX file for a watch, a bike computer, or any GPS that
                reads one, and a FIT course for Garmin. In Garmin Connect, import
                the file under Training, then Courses, and sync. Over USB, copy
                the FIT into <code>Garmin/NewFiles</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                COROS, Suunto, Wahoo, and Hammerhead take the same GPX. A Garmin
                reads the first 15 characters of a course name, so Traceway keeps
                a short device name beside the full one.
            </p>
            <p>
                A multisport plan gives one FIT course for each leg on land,
                named like <code>Brick 2 Run</code>. Start a multisport activity
                on the watch and load each course into its leg. The swim has no
                course, because the watch tracks it without one. The GPX holds
                every leg, swim included, as its own track.
            </p>
            <p>
                In the planner and in your saved routes, Send to device downloads
                the FIT and shows both ways onto a Garmin. A Traceway app for
                Connect IQ, which sends a route over the phone with no cable, is
                on the way.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-cta">
            <a class="fill" href="/dashboard">Open the planner</a>
            <small>Loops for every sport.</small>
        </div>
    </main>
</Base>
